<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">5 November in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">5 events that happened on 5 November, from 1414 to 2006.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/council-of-constance" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/council-of-constance.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1414">1414 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">612 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Council of Constance opens</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A general council met at Constance to end the Great Schism, in which three men claimed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/papacy">papacy</a>. It deposed two, accepted the resignation of the third and elected Martin V, but also condemned <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jan-hus">Jan Hus</a> to the stake.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1605">1605 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">421 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Guy Fawkes is arrested beneath Parliament</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Shortly after midnight, Guy Fawkes was caught guarding <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gunpowder">gunpowder</a> in a cellar under the House of Lords, foiling a Catholic plot to kill James I. Bonfires were lit in celebration, beginning the tradition of Bonfire Night.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1854">1854 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">172 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">British and French troops repel the Russians at Inkerman</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">In thick fog, Russian columns attacked British positions above <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sevastopol">Sevastopol</a>. Fighting in small groups with little direction, the British, reinforced by the French, held the ridge in what became known as the 'Soldiers' Battle'.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1912">1912 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">114 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Woodrow Wilson is elected US president</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">With <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theodore-roosevelt">Theodore Roosevelt</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-howard-taft">William Howard Taft</a> splitting the Republican vote, the Democrat <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/woodrow-wilson">Woodrow Wilson</a> won the presidency. He created the Federal Reserve and led America into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/austro-hungarian-empire">Austro-Hungarian Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/woodrow-wilson">Woodrow Wilson</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/2006">2006 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">20 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Saddam Hussein is sentenced to death</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">An Iraqi tribunal sentenced <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saddam-hussein">Saddam Hussein</a> to hang for the killing of 148 Shia men and boys from Dujail after a 1982 assassination attempt. He was executed on 30 December 2006.</p></div></li></ol>
